From 6ab85d1c42eb8eb92080b0220e81e5ea2bb4f686 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Sat, 13 Jun 2026 16:55:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] patch 0220 -- T68: flip WB cold-init reorder to DEFAULT-ON
 (strict-"0" killswitch)

iter-7 g2k-PROVED the cold-init reorder (patch 0218) kills the WaveBlaster
freeze on the DX2-66 (159 s no-wedge). The iter-4 cold-touch confound that
kept 0218 opt-in/default-OFF is resolved, so the reorder is promoted to the
production default for the wb backend.

Engine half of the shared default-flip: SoundManager's cold-init gate goes
from strict-"1" opt-in (`cold_on = ci && ci[0]=='1'`) to a strict-"0"
KILLSWITCH (`cold_on = !(ci && ci[0]=='0')`): unset / anything-but-"0" =
cold-init ON; explicit "0" forces the old late/blind (hot-bus) init for A/B
+ fallback. New slot (NOT an edit of frozen 0218) per cascade discipline.

LOCKSTEP REQUIREMENT (why this lands FIRST): the cold-init has two halves on
the one hint SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_WB_COLD_INIT -- (1) this engine REORDER
(call SDL_DOSMpu401Init BEFORE MIX_CreateMixerDevice so the bus is COLD) and
(2) sdl-engine's SDL reset/entry/pace sequence. If only the SDL side flips
default-ON without this engine reorder, the default config inits the MPU LATE
(hot bus) and the cold sequence runs HOT = the iter-6 wedge. So the engine
flip must be in the tree before the SDL default flip (sdl T66/0098).

GS-reset (0219) stays default-OFF -- unchanged. Blast radius wb-only
(auto no longer resolves to wb, 0217). Banner "WB COLD-INIT engaged" anchor
preserved for the smoke gate; text updated to say default-ON + killswitch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/sound/SoundManager.cpp | 28 ++++++++++++++++------------
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/sound/SoundManager.cpp b/src/sound/SoundManager.cpp
index 40b0b69f..4e1aebca 100644
--- a/src/sound/SoundManager.cpp
+++ b/src/sound/SoundManager.cpp
@@ -433,19 +433,23 @@ bool SoundManager::init()
   // earlier. selectBackendFromEnv() is pure (env -> enum -> log, no mixer
   // dependency) so it is safe to hoist here from its original post-open position.
   //
-  // OPT-IN, default-OFF (team-lead, per the author-flagged-caveat rule -- an
-  // iter-4 cold-touch wedge confound is weakened but not zero, so opt-in until
-  // the g2k play-through gate passes): the hint SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_WB_COLD_
-  // INIT is strict-"1" to ENGAGE. WCI1 sets it =1 (cold path); WCI0 leaves it
-  // UNSET = today's late-install order = the faithful wedge control (no killswitch
-  // gymnastics). Blast radius is wb-only: auto_select no longer resolves to wb
-  // (patch 0217), and OPL3 / Organya / auto init order is byte-unchanged (their
-  // installs stay in the post-open dispatch switch below).
+  // DEFAULT-ON (patch 0220, T68): iter-7 g2k-PROVED cold-init kills the WB freeze
+  // (159 s no-wedge), so the iter-4 cold-touch confound that kept this opt-in is
+  // resolved and the reorder is now the production default for the wb backend.
+  // The hint SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_WB_COLD_INIT is now a strict-"0" KILLSWITCH:
+  // unset (or anything but "0") = cold-init ON; explicit "0" forces the old
+  // late/blind (hot-bus) init for A/B + fallback. CRITICAL: this flips in lockstep
+  // with sdl-engine's SDL-side cold default (the two halves share the one hint) --
+  // SDL alone default-ON WITHOUT this engine reorder would run the cold sequence
+  // on a HOT bus = the iter-6 wedge, which is why T68 (this engine flip) lands
+  // BEFORE the SDL default flip. Blast radius is wb-only: auto_select no longer
+  // resolves to wb (patch 0217), and OPL3 / Organya / auto init order is
+  // byte-unchanged (their installs stay in the post-open dispatch switch below).
   selectBackendFromEnv();
   bool wb_cold_installed = false;
   {
     const char *ci = SDL_GetHint("SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_WB_COLD_INIT");
-    const bool cold_on = ci && ci[0] == '1' && ci[1] == '\0'; // strict-"1" opt-in
+    const bool cold_on = !(ci && ci[0] == '0' && ci[1] == '\0'); // 0220: default-ON, strict-"0" killswitch
     if (NXE::Diag::g_p10_audio_backend_active == NXE::Diag::AudioBackend::wb &&
         cold_on)
     {
@@ -453,9 +457,9 @@ bool SoundManager::init()
                "SB16 opens (the g2k wedge is the hot UART-entry MPU access while "
                "the SB16 block is live; cold-bus access is probe-safe). The full "
                "cold reset/entry/drain sequence runs in SDL_DOSMpu401Init under "
-               "SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_WB_COLD_INIT; opt-in (=1), unset = today's "
-               "late-install control. Entry-ACK result follows in the SDL WB "
-               "banner (SDL/0095).");
+               "SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_WB_COLD_INIT; DEFAULT-ON (patch 0220), "
+               "killswitch =0 restores the old late/blind init. Entry-ACK result "
+               "follows in the SDL WB banner (SDL/0095).");
       if (_try_install_wb_backend())
       {
         wb_cold_installed = true;
-- 
